Monday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy BLNK calls; CCL calls sold* Stocks slide as coronavirus =
fears re-emerge and stimulus checks questionedStocks are mostly sinking Mon=
day, pulling back from record highs reached last week and as concerns incre=
ased over rises in the rate of COVID-19 infections across the nation amid q=
uestions about the impact of stimulus checks on the economy.In the U.S., th=
e virus "continues to spread unchecked. On average, more than 78 new infect=
ions per 100,000 inhabitants were reported over the last seven days, a new =
record," Commerzbank said in a note on Monday. France, Germany and Italy al=
so saw more infections despite strict restrictions, showing the pandemic re=
mains a global problem.Expectations of stimulus leading to a rise in consum=
ption, as well as about the likelihood that payments may be increased to $2=
,000 after Democratic legislators won two Senate seats in Georgia, helped s=
tocks reach record highs last week.But Commerzbank said surveys showed that=
 "consumers primarily plan to save the $600 they received via checks as par=
t of the latest Corona aid package or use the money to service debt. Few pl=
an additional spending," the report said. "The economic stimulus effect is =
therefore likely to be limited."The Nasdaq Composite, which groups many tec=
hnology stocks, erased Friday gains as it was down Monday with Tesla (TSLA)=
 among the decliners, off 5%. Boeing (BA) fell 2.5% after one of its planes=
 was involved in a fatal crash off the coast of Indonesia on Saturday. Appl=
e (AAPL) fell 1.7%.Twitter (TWTR) tumbled nearly 10% after the social media=
 platform late last week permanently suspended the personal account of U.S.=
 President Donald Trump on security concerns after the rioting on Capitol H=
ill Wednesday. Trump's deleted account had 88 million followers.Tilly's (TL=
YS), a clothing retailer, rose 4% after it reported a 3.3% increase in net =
sales during the 2020 holiday period compared with a year ago. CureVac (CVA=
C) fell 6.2% even after it reported data regarding a COVID-19 vaccine candi=
date in non-human primates.Portfolio: CCL calls stopped out for an 18% loss=
. MCD order did not fill. We have one new recommendation.*CURRENT RECOMMEND=
ATION&nbsp;Carnival Corp. (CCL) January $15 calls-- Symbol: CCL210115C00015=
000-- Bought Jan. 7 at $5.80. -- Sold on stop at $4.85 today Jan 11 at the =
open for an 18% loss.*NEW RECOMMENDATION&nbsp;Blink Charging Co. (BLNK) Feb=
ruary 65 calls-- Symbol: BLNK210219C00065000-- Order: Buy at $5.00 lmt day =
only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $6.50 lmt gtc and half at $8.50 lm=
t gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.50 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Jon=
 D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the thir=
d Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good =
after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are go=
od for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the=
 close of the current session. Past results are no guarantee of future retu=
rns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendations are l=
